{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794382550,"nonce":"JkwdjADtqv8GcrTnEcP5oqfspHA=","message":"Coverage closed, then the LLVM module removed (da15d305, 2fa92115, cd28778d).\n\nInstructions: methods (class, interface, structural), typed and adapted closures, cells and references on a frame at the linker's stack pointer, enums, Dynamic and class casts, Dynamic fields by name, string/bytes constants, narrow unsigned ints, natives of host libraries through their slot, float modulo, virtual closures, Assert, try/catch/rethrow (try_table on __c_longjmp), v128 SIMD (simd primitives, lane reads/writes, auto-vectorizer output). Emitted directly: hello 331/331, Pocket Studio 4038/4038, unit 8688/8688 (after the void-argument fix).\n\nASH_WASM_DIRECT=only builds the whole program with no LLVM module: wasm_program.rs writes the type table, constant pool, runtime tables, ash_module_init, ash_late_init, main, the safe-entry and trap-boundary functions and the call trampolines beside the bodies. A program it cannot take whole (host links, exports, closures, object tails/drops) goes the ordinary way.\n\nVerified: direct-backend tests 11/11 (two new fixtures, TestSimd, whole-program builds without LLVM, each with and without fibers); unit conformance in mixed mode 1069/1069 and 10971/10971 on wasm and wasm-fibers.\n\nNot done: host exports/closures/object tails/drops/host-linked natives (fall back to LLVM); the static-constants blob (constants are built at start-up); 64-bit integer lane min/max reductions. No timing taken yet.","files":null}]}